    {
      "id": "reader_unit_012",
      "section_kind": "interpretive_questions",
      "section_title": "Interpretive Questions",
      "text": "Acts and Galatians differ in selection, emphasis, and sequence when narrating Paul's call and Jerusalem contacts; exact harmonizations remain disputed. Galatians and Acts are independent rhetorical narratives; neither automatic harmonization nor automatic contradiction can replace passage-by-passage comparison.",
