      "section_kind": "interpretive_questions",
      "section_title": "Interpretive Questions",
      "text": "Acts' sequence around Paul's call and Jerusalem visits differs in emphasis and detail from Galatians 1-2, and exact harmonization remains disputed. Acts narrates Paul's encounter three times with rhetorical differences; conversion, prophetic call, and commissioning are overlapping but debated descriptions. Acts presents women as disciples, prophets, patrons, hosts, household leaders, teachers, workers, converts, and sufferers, though narration remains selective and patriarchal constraints persist.",
