      "section_kind": "surrounding_passages",
      "section_title": "Surrounding Passages",
      "text": "Codex Bezae and related versional witnesses preserve a substantially distinctive text of Acts often called Western, whose individual readings require case-by-case judgment. Historical evaluation of Acts must compare particular claims with independent evidence rather than assign blanket reliability or unreliability. Acts is preserved in early papyri and major Greek codices, with P45, P53, P74, Sinaiticus, Vaticanus, and Bezae contributing different portions and textual profiles.",
